---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { cliFilename as filename, cliRun as run } from "../../lib/install";
---
<Base title="Get started"><article class="prose-page"><h1>Start with your project.</h1><p>Diorama UI gives you React components as source. Use your own app, with Tailwind CSS and an <code>@/*</code> alias pointing to your source directory.</p>
<h2 id="install">Diorama CLI</h2><p><a href={`/downloads/${filename}`} download>Download the CLI preview</a> into your project. It installs the source and records what you installed, so later updates can distinguish upstream changes from your own edits.</p><pre class="code-frame">{`${run} init --src src
${run} add theme-zero-css font-aspekta button`}</pre><p><code>init</code> creates <code>ui.config.json</code>. Existing app files stay intact. Use <code>--src</code> to match your app’s source directory and configure the same alias in your framework.</p><p>The package reports any npm dependencies you need to install. The public npm release is being prepared as <code>@bydiorama/ui</code>; the downloadable preview runs without a repository checkout.</p>
<h2>Load the foundations</h2><p>Import <code>src/styles/theme-zero.css</code> after Tailwind. Load <code>/fonts/aspekta/aspekta.css</code>, and <a href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bydiorama/ui/main/registry/fonts/aspekta/AspektaVF.woff2">download the Aspekta font</a> beside it in <code>public/fonts/aspekta/</code>. Keep its OFL notice there.</p>
<h2 id="shadcn">Existing shadcn apps</h2><p>The shadcn CLI remains an alternative. Add the namespace below to <code>components.json</code>, then install the parts you need.</p><pre class="code-frame">{JSON.stringify({ registries: { "@bydiorama": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bydiorama/ui/main/r/{name}.json" } }, null, 2)}</pre><pre class="code-frame">npx shadcn@latest add @bydiorama/button</pre><p>Our CLI also reads an existing <code>components.json</code>. Running <code>init</code> retains its aliases, so you can adopt the owned channel gradually.</p>
<h2>Keep the source yours</h2><p>Read it, adapt it, and keep the typed documentation beside it. Use <code>sync</code> to review upstream changes before replacing code you have modified.</p><p><a href="/components/">Browse components</a> · <a href="/docs/agents/">Build with an agent</a></p></article></Base>
